{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"blueblack-piecemeal-equine","creation_channel":"cli","description":"# Context\nOperator-approved (2026-08-12): make ticket-directory creation atomic so interrupted-write debris cannot occur. Evidence: fsck found 8 empty stray ticket dirs (MISSING_CREATE + FOREIGN_STORE_PATH), all the `makedirs`-then-die signature — the dir existed before its CREATE event file did, and interruptions (host sleep, process kill, timeout) in that window strand a plausible-looking empty ticket dir in the tracker working tree. Swept manually via tracker-maintenance --clean under ticket illsuited-erect-ibis (7c6e-4b8a-59c5-46db); the reducer's tolerance ruling (bug 043f: \"tolerate, never tidy\") deliberately rejects automatic cleanup, so prevention at the writer is the self-healing fix.\n\nDesign direction: stage the new ticket dir + its CREATE event file in a temp path inside the tracker (same filesystem — e.g. a dot-prefixed sibling the store scanner ignores and FOREIGN_STORE_PATH won't flag as a ticket), then `os.rename` into the final ticket-id path. Rename is atomic on the same filesystem: an interruption leaves only the ignorable temp path, never a bare ticket dir. Consider the same window for any other dir-then-first-file creation in the store write path (e.g. session-log rotation, sidecar dirs) — fix the class, not just CREATE, where the same signature exists.\n\n# Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] AC1 — Ticket creation stages dir+CREATE atomically: killing the writer at any point between staging start and rename leaves NO path that fsck reports as MISSING_CREATE/FOREIGN_STORE_PATH (temp paths are excluded from both checks by naming convention, documented).\n- [ ] AC2 — A RED test simulates the interruption (kill/exception injected between mkdir and event write in the OLD code shape) proving the debris signature, and the fix turns it green; a rename-crash test proves the temp path is invisible to fsck and cleaned on the next writer's start (bounded, best-effort temp sweep of stale temp paths owned by dead pids — this does not violate 043f since temp paths are the writer's own staging area, not store data).\n- [ ] AC3 — Concurrency: two concurrent creates of different tickets don't collide on temp paths (pid/uuid-suffixed staging names); the existing write-lock discipline is unchanged.\n- [ ] AC4 — Any other same-signature dir-then-file sites in the store write path are converted or explicitly recorded as exempt with reasons.\n- [ ] AC5 — make lint/typecheck pass; store suite green; no change to event formats or committed layout.","id":"021d-ae08-ecd6-4495","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"task","title":"Atomic ticket-dir creation: eliminate interrupted-write debris"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1786584263162791001,"uuid":"667fc825-f82e-49be-a5ec-e776974236bd"}